they didn't. So internet forums of stock investors were complete chaos, starting all sorts of rumors as stocks continue to fall. And I remember realizing the power of this financial panic, and I was panicking as well. And it was one of those short but pivotal moments, I think, that I realized that I didn't want my emotions to be tied to the state of the stock market. And soon after that, I applied to grad school and became a researcher of that phenomena. But I vividly remember that experience.

