of what is about to happen. I think that makes things so much stronger. I want to go a little bit further back in history. During World War II, Japan bombed Pearl Harbor. And shortly after that, fears about Japanese-Americans spread like wildfire across the United States. It's somewhat hard to imagine today, but thousands upon thousands of Japanese-American citizens

