about the individual tree. You have to be taking a broader view and thinking of the collective phenomena here and how you take control of that. And so that's one insight of because emotions spread, they become more intense. A related idea is that collective emotions change what gets shared and expressed. So we've talked about the idea that more extreme emotions in some ways attract attention, but can you say a moment about the valence of that emotion? What happens when the emotion being expressed is positive versus negative? So one of the most basic findings in emotion research is what we call negativity bias,

